Dock keystone: mission-control overview (expo), from the upstream patch. A 5-finger
gesture (`overview` action, in both config front-ends) or hl.dsp.overview() toggles
it: ksOverviewToggle() collects every mapped, non-pinned window across all
workspaces; while active, renderMonitor() draws the live workspace, then
renderOverview() as an overlay -- the wallpaper dimmed, each window's live surface
texture in a grid tile (texture-direct, since off-workspace windows render blank
through renderWindow, but their last committed buffer is kept). A click jumps to the
tile's workspace, focuses it and closes. Direct scanout and the solitary-client fast
path are off while it is up.

